# Profile design language

A 2007 SpaceHey/MySpace profile crossed with a Nirvana/Deftones gig flyer:
cream cards on black, barcode ticks, grain, tiled stars, restrained glitch.
Not cyberpunk. Not glassy.

Layout source of truth: the uploaded `Das Profile.dc.html` Design Component
(black page, cream panels, 280px left column, interests in the right column,
social 3×2 grid, `[edit]` in the About header).

## Stack

SvelteKit + Svelte 5 runes (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`) + TypeScript.
Static adapter. No CSS framework.

## Svelte 5 (from NIL)

- Props: `let { ... }: Props = $props();` with an explicit `interface Props`.
- No `export let`, no `$:` labels, no `on:click` — events are attributes.
- Children use snippets, not slots.
- Exhaustive `switch` over unions with a `never` default.
- Imports stay at the top of the file.

## Tokens

Hex lives only in `src/lib/styles/tokens.css`. Components consume
`var(--color-*)` / `var(--font-*)` / `var(--s-*)`. Locked casual core:

```css
--font-display: 'Anton', Impact, sans-serif;
--font-body: 'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif;
--color-bg: #050505;
--color-panel: #ece7dd;
--color-panel-ink: #111111;
--color-ink: #e8e4dc;
--color-red: #e01b2e;
```

`--color-ink` is cream text on black. Titles on cream panels use
`--color-panel-ink`, never `--color-ink`.

Motion keyframes live in `src/lib/styles/motion.css`. Honor
`prefers-reduced-motion`.

## What makes it alive

1. Real photos in `static/photos/`, referenced from `profile.ts` as
   `{ src, alt, rotate, ... }` and treated automatically in `PhotoScatter`.
2. Small ambient motion only: grain drift, star field, rare name glitch (~7s),
   photo parallax on pointer. Nothing looping wall-to-wall.
3. Asymmetry: rotated polaroids, barcode ticks, uneven widget cards.

## Themes

`document.documentElement.dataset.theme` is `casual` | `pro`. Casual is this
black/white/red page. Pro is a clean portfolio skin keyed off the same data.

## Page is a layout file

Content lives in `src/lib/data/profile.ts`. Components take props. Do not
hardcode copy into markup.
